# One TOC for every client: retail (game type "standard"), WoW Forever
# ("camelot"), Mists, TBC Anniversary and Classic Era. Each client loads only
# its own skin manifest, picked per line with load directives, the same way
# Blizzard's own TOCs split per flavor.
#
# The Forever line carries the extra Exclude because clients that do not know
# the camelot token treat an unknown AllowLoadGameType as a match. The other
# tokens (standard, classic, mists, tbc, vanilla) are known to every client.
#
# RequiredDeps skips Forever, which lacks several of the Blizzard_Deprecated*
# shims. LoadWith is retail-only: Blizzard_EncounterJournal never loads on
# Forever, and the classic flavors never had the line.

libs\Libs.xml
Skin\skin.xml
Skin\Interface\AddOns\AddOns_Mainline.xml [AllowLoadGameType standard]
Skin\Interface\AddOns\AddOns_Forever.xml [AllowLoadGameType camelot][ExcludeLoadGameType standard, classic]
Skin\Interface\AddOns\AddOns_Mists.xml [AllowLoadGameType mists]
Skin\Interface\AddOns\AddOns_TBC.xml [AllowLoadGameType tbc]
Skin\Interface\AddOns\AddOns_Vanilla.xml [AllowLoadGameType vanilla]

config.lua
analytics.lua
compatibility.lua
integration.lua
aurora.lua
gui.lua

#@do-not-package@
dev\test.lua
#@end-do-not-package@
